  "response": {
    "html": "<h1 data-chunk-id=\"3bc2996f-bc9c-4952-94e4-082cb929614d\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;border-bottom:3px solid #0d47a1;padding-bottom:6px\">Nebula Drift - Game Design Document</h1>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"e85a2279-e23a-4e18-844e-471adb111dd9\" style=\"background-color:#e3f2fd;border-left:4px solid #1565c0;padding:8px 10px;font-size:9pt;color:#37474f\">Vantage Nine Studios - internal - the spine. Numbers live in Mechanics; do not duplicate them here except as prose.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"690a3043-57f1-422c-9b42-0bff9c860d86\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Overview</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"8aa78be2-f3af-46d1-a452-4517745a2060\">Nebula Drift is a single-player momentum-platformer set in the wreckage of a\ncollapsed orbital shipyard. The player is a salvager who cannot fight most of\nwhat lives there and must out-move it instead.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"7d09fbcb-728d-42ce-bea2-ba6b05fde237\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Design pillars</h2>\n<ul data-chunk-id=\"5d10bab7-9218-402e-b130-9aa848ee78ea\">\n<li><strong>Momentum is the reward.</strong> Every system either preserves speed or\nexplains clearly why it took it away.</li>\n<li><strong>The wreck remembers.</strong> Sections the player has stripped stay stripped.</li>\n<li><strong>Legibility over spectacle.</strong> If a hazard cannot be read in one frame at\nspeed, it is cut.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"77ce8216-da52-454a-82eb-10cedd815093\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Core loop</h2>\n<ol data-chunk-id=\"cf007335-9d1d-452e-9f70-c2bae337bd8b\">\n<li>Enter a sector and read its silhouette for salvage.</li>\n<li>Route through it without stopping.</li>\n<li>Strip what you reached; lose what you did not.</li>\n<li>Spend salvage on traversal upgrades, never on combat.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"4c6e42c3-2a33-481a-8296-95b094c2854c\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Traversal</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"a611e8b5-3ee8-4319-8bda-dc9c71a12f99\">Traversal is the game. The player has a dash, a wall-run and a grapple. The\ngrapple is the only tool that converts height into speed, so it carries the\nlongest cooldown in the game at <strong>8 s</strong>, and every level is paced\naround that number.</p>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"6df33df0-52ce-46d2-87a8-2b18de3df272\">Full parameters live in the Mechanics sub-document, section \"Grapple\".</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"d6c0a908-c8b8-4cd6-baae-df40597fb4a2\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Combat</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"c6a693c2-8b76-49e9-a7eb-bd39f3291e1a\">Combat exists to make traversal mistakes expensive. The player has one\ndefensive tool - an overheat pulse - and no weapons.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"77c3b380-6a74-4a3a-ae95-53843d17ecac\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Progression</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"083f739e-9fa8-4c99-999e-adbe0c78516a\">Salvage buys traversal upgrades in a flat, non-branching order. No skill tree:\nthe team has shipped one before and it cost six weeks of tuning for no measured\nretention gain.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"a22a6b71-62ac-4142-90c3-5eeb2488316a\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Art direction</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"8e392936-cebd-472c-997f-b4f7a8f882a9\">Readable-industrial. Detail lives in silhouette, not surface. Full rules,\npalette and reference boards live in the Art Bible sub-document.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"3130001f-5382-4bd3-bf92-6b81dd4d22c5\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Narrative</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"32bb9fc3-6db1-44ef-8ac6-84e1aae06391\">Told through the wreck itself and one voice on a dying channel. Beat sheet\nand characters live in the Narrative sub-document.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"3088549b-7efb-454a-87ab-48865d0f168f\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Linked sub-documents</h2>\n<table data-chunk-id=\"26724c8f-09f5-4d49-8361-5f9cba89f0e2\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #37474f;font-family:Inter , Calibri , Arial , sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"><thead><tr>\n<th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Sub-document</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Owns</th>\n<th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Sections in this GDD that depend on it</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Mechanics</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Every tunable number</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Traversal, Combat, Progression</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Narrative</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Acts, beats, characters</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Narrative</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Art Bible</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Palette, silhouette rules, concept art</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Art direction</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"58198ad8-4271-4159-ab74-54fb501b678d\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Open questions</h2>\n<ul data-chunk-id=\"d4148054-c51b-4fa6-a3b6-841d211c95f8\">\n<li>Does the overheat pulse need a resource cost, or is the cooldown enough?</li>\n<li>Can a sector be re-entered after it is stripped, and does that break pillar 2?</li>\n</ul>",
